    {
      "id": "67381d714631f80039c2f9f7925f563cd9f83d8a",
      "tag": "autogenerated:ai-review",
      "author": {
        "_account_id": 1345,
        "name": "Gerrit AI review for Lustre",
        "display_name": "AI review",
        "email": "gaireview@linuxhacker.ru",
        "username": "aireview",
        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-11-06 09:06:59.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 2:\n\n(10 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nSome concerns, see inline comments: this needs a refresh for the three defects (the cursor lost on a failed read, chunks dropped when a read fails, and cursor identity), and the inline minors can ride along.\n\ntest8 only runs on the conf-sanity 300a/300b fixture, whose EAs are small, so the jumbo, -EOVERFLOW and non-jumbo skip paths of lfu_fill_inode() don't appear to be exercised, and neither is LFU_FEATURE_SKIPPED or a read that fails. The shard check also only offers a cursor from a whole-target stream, so dc_shard_index is never what refuses it. Could test8 add an object with an EA larger than the read (a long linkea from many hard links, for example), and a read with a cursor from a sibling shard?",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 2
    },
