        "subject": "LU-20730 llapi: read a device scan as LFU chunks",
        "message": "LU-20730 llapi: read a device scan as LFU chunks\n\nllapi_scan_device() calls back once per object, so a consumer that\nwants objects in bulk, to write them out or hand them to another\nprocess or node, copies each record into a batch of its own.\n\nAdd llapi_lfu_open(), llapi_lfu_read(), llapi_lfu_info() and\nllapi_lfu_close(), the LfuOpen/LfuRead/LfuClose operation of\nlfu.capnp as a function call. Each read fills the caller's buffer\nwith whole LfuChunk slots, written in place by the codec, and returns\nthe cursor to go on from. The first source is LFU_SOURCE_DEVICE.\n\nA device stream reads in the caller's thread with one backend worker.\nParallelism is by shard: shard i of n is the i-th n-th of the\nbackend's units of work. A cursor names a unit and the first object\nid in it not yet sent, so a read stops when the buffer is full and\nthe next read, or a new stream after a restart, resumes at that\nobject; ids below it are dropped before any xattr is read. A cursor\nanother target or shard wrote is -ESTALE.\n\nRecords carry the inode's own attributes and the EAs the demand mask\nneeds, as stored: trusted.fid names an OST object's file. An object\nwithout a FID is counted, not sent: the stream names objects by FID,\nand has no field for the target's own id, so lli_want never has\nLLAPI_SCAN_INO. An object too large for a slot gets a jumbo chunk if\nthe consumer reads them, otherwise it is counted in the chunk's errors\nand named in its skipped list. scan_obj_fid() is split out of\nscan_sink_object() so both paths compute the FID the same way.\n\nllapi_scan_device_test test8, run by conf-sanity 300a and 300b,\nreads the MDT and an OST in 3-slot reads of 4 KiB and checks that the\nstream sends exactly the objects llapi_scan_device() delivers, also\nwhen resumed on a new stream and when read as 3 shards, and that\nforeign cursors and bad parameters are refused.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=300a,300b\nSigned-off-by: Artem Blagodarenko <ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm\nChange-Id: I73f7520820ff547d6fe9d6c8d6f851624c4b83c7\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
